            "text": "{\"strengths\":[\"The diagram correctly shows unchanged demand and a leftward shift of supply from S1 to S2 in the wheat market.\",\"Both equilibria are identified and the diagram clearly shows P2 above P1 and Q2 left of Q1.\",\"The explanation gives a complete causal chain from drought and reduced harvests to shortage, a higher equilibrium price and lower quantity traded.\"],\"improvements\":[],\"mistakes\":[],\"examinerComment\":\"Estimated practice result: 4/4. Your diagram and explanation are fully consistent. You accurately explain that the drought reduces supply at every price while demand remains unchanged, causing a shortage at the original equilibrium price and movement to a new equilibrium with higher price and lower quantity traded.\",\"studyNext\":\"Practise explaining the opposite supply shift: how improved harvest conditions would affect equilibrium price and quantity when demand is unchanged.\",\"assessmentFormat\":\"paper_2_c_to_f_diagram_and_explanation\",\"paper\":\"paper_2\",\"questionPart\":\"unknown\",\"levelRelevance\":\"shared_sl_hl\",\"assessmentSkills\":[\"diagram_explanation\",\"economic_analysis\",\"application\"],\"commandTerm\":\"explain\",\"commandTermLabel\":\"Using a demand and supply diagram, explain\",\"syllabusUnit\":\"unit_2\",\"syllabusTopic\":\"2.3\",\"topicLabel\":\"Competitive market equilibrium\",\"classificationConfidence\":\"high\",\"markingConfidence\":\"high\",\"diagramExpected\":true,\"diagramSubmitted\":true,\"diagramAssessmentStatus\":\"submitted_and_assessed\",\"workingsExpected\":false,\"workingsSubmitted\":false,\"workingsAssessmentStatus\":\"not_relevant\",\"attachmentContent\":\"diagram\",\"assessableEarned\":4,\"markBreakdown\":[{\"label\":\"Diagram\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"The readable diagram identifies the wheat market, conventional price and quantity axes, unchanged D, S1 and left-shifted S2, and two equilibria showing P2 higher than P1 and Q2 lower than Q1.\"},{\"label\":\"Economic analysis\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"The written explanation accurately links reduced harvests to lower supply at each price, shortage at P1, a price rise, and a lower equilibrium quantity traded.\"},{\"label\":\"Application to context\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"The explanation is consistently applied to the stated drought in the wheat market and correctly holds demand unchanged.\"}],\"bandRationale\":null,\"limitations\":[],\"componentEvaluation\":{\"diagram\":2,\"explanation\":2,\"diagramReason\":\"A fully identifiable supply contraction is shown against unchanged demand, with both demand-supply intersections and correctly directed equilibrium price and quantity outcomes.\",\"explanationReason\":\"The response provides the complete drought-to-reduced-supply-to-shortage-to-new-equilibrium causal chain, reaching higher price and lower quantity traded.\",\"incompatibleMechanisms\":false,\"mismatchEvidence\":\"\",\"labelingDeficiency\":false,\"labelingEvidence\":\"\",\"rootErrors\":[]}}"
